<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Tradeable premium band for a config's option legs.

      Purpose
      =======
      itm_depth / otm_depth decide WHICH strikes are scanned; these decide which
      of them are worth entering. The two are not interchangeable: a strike that
      is one step OTM in the morning can be worth 200 points, and the same strike
      near expiry can be worth 6.

      Without a band, a SELL config with target/stop_loss expressed as absolute
      points behaves incoherently across the premium range it scans. Selling a
      6.35 option, the most that can ever be earned is 6.35 - premium decaying to
      zero - so a 30-point target can never fire, while a 30-point stop is 472%
      of the premium. On the same tick the deep-ITM leg at 254 has that same
      30-point stop sitting at 12%, i.e. ordinary noise.

      Both bounds are nullable and independent: NULL means unbounded on that
      side, so every config that predates this change keeps its exact behaviour.
      Checked at signal generation against the leg's premium at that moment, and
      only for signals that would OPEN a position - see Strategy1.
    -->
    <changeSet id="024_add_option_price_range_to_trade_config" author="moneymaker">
        <addColumn tableName="trade_config">
            <column name="min_option_price" type="DECIMAL(12,4)"/>
            <column name="max_option_price" type="DECIMAL(12,4)"/>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
